  "status": "draft",
  "description": "Chronic kidney disease (KDIGO): enrolled by N18, or by an eGFR below 60 or a urine albumin/creatinine ratio of 30 mg/g or more on two results at least 90 days apart. Creatinine/eGFR and urine albumin/creatinine ratio as often as the KDIGO 2012 heat map asks for the patient's stage (1 to 4 times a year: G3a A1 yearly, G4 every 3 to 4 months), and a control visit every 6 months up to G3a, every 4 months at G3b, every 3 months at G4-G5. Fills only what the doctor's plan did not cover.",
  "reason": {
    "code": "protocol_chronic_kidney_disease",
    "label": "Control de enfermedad renal crónica"
  },
